cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "convexity: quantitative finance analytics with explicit conventions"
message: "If you use this software in research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Oyeyemi
    given-names: Demi
    email: oyeyemidemilade@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/demilade-o/convexity"
url: "https://github.com/demilade-o/convexity"
abstract: >-
  An open-source Python library for quantitative finance analytics. Provides
  performance, risk, drawdown and risk-adjusted return metrics with documented
  formulas, explicit conventions, and honest failure modes. Annualisation,
  compounding, day count, risk-free treatment and missing-data policy are
  explicit parameters rather than silent defaults; where the literature offers
  competing definitions, the variants are exposed and the default is documented
  with its source. The computational core performs no network I/O; data
  retrieval lives behind optional, provenance-bearing provider adapters.
keywords:
  - quantitative finance
  - performance analytics
  - risk
  - drawdown
  - Sortino ratio
  - Calmar ratio
  - Sharpe ratio
  - risk-free rate
  - Python
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
